.TH FOOBAR 1 "" "foobar @VERSION@"
.SH NAME
foobar \- Print a greeting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B foobar
.RB [ \-hVs ]
.RB [ \-\-usage ]
.PP
.B foobar
.RB [ \-s ]
.B alpha
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR MESSAGE ]
.RB [ \-\-usage ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The alpha subcommand prints MESSAGE followed by a newline when provided.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit. Also accepted after alpha for subcommand help.
.TP
.B \-\-usage
Print a brief usage message and exit. Also accepted after alpha.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit. This is a global option, before any command.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
Suppress message output. This is a global option, before the command.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-message " MESSAGE"
Set the message. This option belongs to alpha and follows the command name.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 for invalid arguments or an output error.
